## Definition of done (every change)
Functional code changes follow `{{RULES_DIR}}/functionality-first-delivery.<ext>`: intended behavior proven — ideally on the real surface — before hardening or broad audits; pre-acceptance auditor findings queue; docs/mocks/planning are exempt.
Architecture still coherent; the intended source of truth drives the final user-visible behavior; tests prove product logic not just compilation; blast-radius docs updated if a relation was exposed; {{SAFETY_INVARIANTS}} preserved where applicable; security/privacy/tenant-isolation considered; any deferred follow-up named with a reason, never silently dropped.

For visible frontend work, load the global `frontend-design-director` before any prompt, mock, critique, or implementation. Route marketing/editorial surfaces to `design-taste-frontend` and dashboards, admin, analytics, or product workflows to `product-ui-design-taste`; preserve the project's mock-approval gate.

When a skill used in a task exposes a proven reusable loophole, trigger/routing miss, stale rule, or better method, load the global `skill-evolution-loop` and patch the canonical owning skill/trigger/rubric/test in the same task with a fail-state, regression mutation, counterexample, validation, and behavioral re-test. Keep project-specific lessons local and preserve human approval for material doctrine/safety changes.
